course: dictionary
lesson: 8186
title: Responsible
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Responsible is an adjective with three main meanings, and the words around it tell you which one you need. Look for clues about jobs, blame, or trust. «You are responsible for feeding the fish» means feeding the fish is your job.
explain: Responsible can also mean that you caused something, so you can be blamed or praised for it. «A dare does not make a rude act acceptable; the person who does it is still responsible.» The clues are the dare and the rude act: the person who did it is the one who must answer for it.
explain: A responsible person is sensible and can be trusted to do the right thing. «Both come from the same place: a big sister feeling responsible for you.» Swap in "feeling in charge of you" and see if it still makes sense. It does, so you have found the meaning.
fact: Responsible means it is your job or duty to look after something or to do it.
fact: If you are responsible for something that happened, you caused it and can be blamed or praised.
fact: A responsible person is sensible and can be trusted to do the right thing.
fact: «Telling the owner about a weakness without using it is called responsible disclosure.»
fact: The phrase «take responsibility» means you accept your part in something that happened.
exercise: «You are responsible for feeding the fish.» What does responsible mean here? | It means you caused the fish to be hungry | It means you like fish | It means you are sensible about fish | *It is your job to look after the fish
exercise: «A dare does not make a rude act acceptable; the person who does it is still responsible.» Here, responsible means | *The person caused it and can be blamed | The person is very sensible | It is a job someone must do | The person was chosen to lead
exercise: Which word in «Telling the owner about a weakness without using it is called responsible disclosure.» means someone can be trusted to do the right thing? | owner | disclosure | weakness | *responsible
test: «Both come from the same place: a big sister feeling responsible for you.» What does responsible mean? | She is wearing a school uniform | *She feels she must look after you | She is tall and strong | She caused you to be upset
test: Which sentence shows a person who caused something bad and can be blamed? | A responsible pupil always finishes homework | Mum is responsible for the washing up on Sundays | Sam feels happy about the new fish | *Liam knocked over the vase, so he is responsible for the mess
exam: Which meaning fits a responsible person who can be trusted? | *Sensible and able to be trusted to do the right thing | Someone who is very loud | Someone who is always late | A person who is fast at running
